dot/pull/113861.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-06T18:44:27Z"},"body":"## Issue description\r\n\r\n1. Create a 2D scene with the Compatibility renderer\r\n2. Add a WorldEnvironment node with an Environment\r\n3. Change Background mode to Canvas\r\n4. Change the tonemapper to one that is not Linear\r\n5. Note that the tonemapper is not applied\r\n6. Enable Glow\r\n7. Note that the tonemapper is now applied\r\n\r\n## This PR\r\n\r\n- Fixes (partially) #110902 (half of this issue)\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes the above problem by applying tonemapping the same way that Glow is applied when using a Canvas background mode with the Compatibility renderer.\r\n\r\nI also renamed a variable to keep the code clean, which makes this PR appear larger than it absolutely needs to be.\r\n\r\n## Outstanding issues\r\n\r\nThere is another outstanding issue relating to how Tonemap Exposure should be applied when background mode is Canvas, but I think this is best left to a separate PR, as the fix is quite a bit more complex and nuanced...\r\n\r\nUpdate: My solution to this issue with exposure is here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113863","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/recei